Presence of this file opts the project into the protoblast plugin's checkNativeNumberInputs
and checkNativeNumberInputTemplates compile gates (no Java source and no .hwk template may
produce a native numeric input -- that control reads the BROWSER's UI locale for its decimal
separator rather than the page's, so it refuses or misreads what a localized page told the
reader to type, and nothing objects; render pl-number-input or pl-money-input instead, see
CheckNativeNumberInputsTask).

Opted in 2026-09-23, when the last native numeric control (the TTL of a secondary zone's
remote record form) moved to pl-number-input. The guard sees only its declared literal
shapes; a type reached through a constant or a variable still has to be checked by eye.
